:"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"14caf739d4a7aa32d38320ba4884a4c1880d8cab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/commits/14caf739d4a7aa32d38320ba4884a4c1880d8cab","html_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/commit/14caf739d4a7aa32d38320ba4884a4c1880d8cab"}]},{"sha":"8568549c93a404df415244053affda5df02eb8e1","node_id":"C_kwDOAA3dP9oAKDg1Njg1NDljOTNhNDA0ZGY0MTUyNDQwNTNhZmZkYTVkZjAyZWI4ZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matt Haberland","email":"mhaberla@calpoly.edu","date":"2023-11-11T06:46:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2023-11-11T06:46:41Z"},"message":"DOC: standardize capitalization of NEP headings (#25060)\n\nMore toward gh-16261.\r\n\r\ngh-16261 reported that documentation headings currently have inconsistent capitalization schemes and should be standardized. gh-25016 fixed this for rst files except release notes and NEPS. This PR adjusts the NEPs.\r\n\r\nThe case of 'numpy', 'blas', 'scipy', 'python', 'lapack', 'fortran', 'api', 'pypi', 'cpu', 'abi', 'pr', 'github', 'ssh', 'git', 'f77', 'numba', 'f2py', 'cffi', 'bitgenerator', 'simd', 'swig', 'csv', 'ascii', 'json', 'dataframe', 'ieee', 'matlab', 'pyfort', ' c ', and 'nep' are unchanged. (Perhaps it would be a good idea to check the capitalization of some of these words throughout the documentation, but that is a different issue.)","tree":{"sha":"ef8c55137ac688a73bb18ad98e74e87119b7f866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/git/trees/ef8c55137ac688a73bb18ad98e74e87119b7f866"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/git/commits/8568549c93a404df415244053affda5df02eb8e1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJlTyNRCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAA5EQIAAZCe8GHPoE8k7Pmpa/FGRaj\nO99vUuZuooJWVNhuj2oxPoC8yPdS8sgI9izE8OGStukPtob9AUS5xn6PAdZAT2y4\n9gpfBnW1cH0fJ8jS/0uSIKOprNcTbMZgDoW+G1DXiuSfflTYumVgB4tEsEJIQlts\ngw9ctjalKSaBl0bqMFPjhLLGdCPUArtLlGd